      "content": "To set your safety stock, multiply your lead time by the standard deviation of demand during that period, then add the result to your average demand. A more robust approach is to use a service-focused formula: Park's formula, which multiplies the standard deviation of demand during lead time by a factor of your desired service level, usually around 30 to 40 kg per square meter for high-variability items like your batteries. This ensures you have enough buffer stock to absorb spikes without stockouts during busy periods.",
